Rebrand VS Code surfaces to Composery (identity, assets, theme cache)

VS Code-only patch. The code-server src/node env var, path, and template token
renames (CODE_SERVER_*/CS_* -> COMPOSERY_*, code-server -> composery paths,
{{CS_STATIC_BASE}} -> {{COMPOSERY_STATIC_BASE}}) live in the src-node-*.diff
patches. This patch covers:

- product.json identity and links (ci/build/build-vscode.sh): adds
  serverDataFolderName -> ".composery-server", repoints the Microsoft docs/tips/
  videos/newsletter links to composery.io, and adds https://www.composery.io to
  linkProtectionTrustedDomains so opening the brand link (e.g. the title-bar
  logo's "Open Link in New Tab") never prompts. nameShort/nameLong and the
  license/report-issue URLs are left as upstream context: rebrand.mjs already
  rewrites them (code-server -> Composery, coder GitHub URLs -> sloikodavid),
  so patching them here would double-maintain the same rename. Internal ids
  (applicationName, win32/darwin, keyboard-shortcut PDFs) stay code-server.
- product logo and letterpress (lib/vscode .../code-icon.svg + editor/sessions
  letterpress svgs): VS Code icon and empty-editor/sessions watermarks -> Composery
  icon. Patched in source, not overlaid, because the minified build relocates them.
- theme cache (lib/vscode .../workbenchThemeService.ts): force one
  reloadCurrentColorTheme() after init so a rebuilt Composery theme overrides the
  colours VS Code persists in browser IndexedDB.
- client identity (lib/vscode .../workbench/browser/client.ts): the insecure-context
  warning names "Composery" instead of "code-server" and offers the standard
  persistent "Don't Show Again" action; the upstream code-server
  release notifier is removed entirely (the composery-updates builtin extension is
  the single, properly-branded update notifier, so the upstream one was a duplicate
  that branded the product "code-server" and linked to cdr/code-server); and the
  Sign-out / Reset-password / Show-QR command ids move out of the shared code-server.*
  namespace to composery.* (composery.logout, composery.resetPassword, composery.qr.show
  - .qr.show avoids colliding with the composery.showQr id owned by composery-qr).

The CLI binary, IPC socket/mutex names, /tmp scratch dir, version coordinates, and
upstream artifact/env names are intentionally left untouched (build/runtime machinery,
never user-visible). The update-check route (src-node overlay, routes/index.ts) is
repointed from coder/code-server to the Composery repo now that the notification it
fed is Composery-branded. See README "Branding rename policy".

